  "id": "spiritlevel",
  "neon": "#ffd27a",
  "note": "SPIRIT LEVEL — the off-licence at the bottom of Ironside, the last shop before the South Gate.\n\nThe tile's prose: the whole frontage is behind a folding grille, the window behind the grille is\nglass block, and the only opening is a hatch cut in a steel shutter at chest height, lit from\ninside, with a lipped sill and a turntable so that nothing passes hand to hand. After dark the\nhatch is the only lit thing on the road and the shop behind it is black.\n\nSo the front is a steel shutter across the ground floor with the hatch in it, a band of glass\nblock above, and a rank of grille bars standing off both. The name is painted on the parapet band\n(`off_licence` is a `painted` fascia) and nothing else on the building is lit. The flanks\nare blank brick with a downpipe and a vent each.\n\nIt binds by name and replaces no named arm; `type:off_licence` keeps its arm for any other\noff-licence.",
